# Feature branch workflow

Every feature or fix must follow this flow. Do **not** commit directly to `main`.

## Branch

1. Create a branch from `main`: `feat/<short-name>`, `fix/<short-name>`, or `chore/<short-name>`
2. Keep scope focused (one feature per branch)
3. Commits: English, [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)

## Validation

1. Run `make lint` (helm lint + template default + gateway profile)
2. Deploy and test on a **Kubernetes cluster** before opening a PR when behavior changes
3. Document what was tested in the PR body

## Merge

1. Open a PR to `main` — do **not** merge without maintainer approval
2. Maintainer validates on a cluster and approves merge
3. After merge: push git tag `v*` to publish chart to GitHub Pages and rebuild docs at `/docs/`

See `.cursor/rules/versioning.mdc` for SemVer policy (aligned with `core` app repo).

## Cross-repo features

When core app and chart change together, use the same branch name in both repos and deploy from the chart repo with sibling `../core` checkout.
